<article class="env-remark" id="0DKZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DKZ">Remark <span data-tag="0DKZ">76.52.12</span>.</a> The reader may have noticed the similarity between Lemma <a href="/tag/0DKY" data-tag="0DKY">76.52.11</a> and Derived Categories of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/08JR" data-tag="08JR">75.23.3</a>. Indeed, the pseudo-coherent complex $L$ of Lemma <a href="/tag/0DKY" data-tag="0DKY">76.52.11</a> may be characterized as the unique pseudo-coherent complex on $Y$ such that there are functorial isomorphisms </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^ i_{\mathcal{O}_ Y}(L, \mathcal{F}) \longrightarrow \mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^ i_{\mathcal{O}_ X}(K, E \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ X}^\mathbf {L} Lf^*\mathcal{F})  \]
</div>
  <p> compatible with boundary maps for $\mathcal{F}$ ranging over $\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ Y)$. If we ever need this we will formulate a precise result here and give a detailed proof. </p>
</article>